# CANONICAL §7.6 fixture — `PreviewOp` echoes the mate-resolved placement
# (additive optional `result.matePlacement`, same shape as §7.2
# `planStep.matePlacement`) whenever the candidate PlaceComponent's mate RESOLVED,
# whether or not the seat moved (present <=> resolved in this preview).
#
#   1. MATED, off the plane. The M6 screw is drafted at z=0 but mated COINCIDENT
#      to the plate's top face (z=5): the preview re-seats it ON the plane, so the
#      result carries `matePlacement.translate` z = 5 exactly (a plane-to-plane
#      distance between faces the extrude placed at z=0 / z=5; no measured float).
#   2. UNMATED. No mate: `matePlacement` is ABSENT. The harness matcher is
#      subset-only and cannot assert absence, so the absence is pinned by the Rust
#      real-worker test (`component_placement_pipeline.rs`) and by `GetWorkerHead`
#      below proving the head is untouched; this leg pins that the unmated preview
#      still succeeds with the unchanged result keys.
#   3. MATED, UNMOVED. Drafted exactly on the plane (z=5): the echo is PRESENT with
#      the resolved placement (translate z = 5).
#
# GEOMETRY as in place_component_mate_reseat.ndjson: plate x∈[−20,0], y∈[0,40],
# z∈[0,5]; Ø6 cylinder through (100,0).
# The plate (5 mm) and the cylinder, one plan.
